IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `acc-types`
IMPORT `acc-cover`
IMPORT `acc-claims-disputes`
IMPORT `acc-entitlements`
IMPORT `acc-levies-offences`

-- Accident Compensation Act 2001 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this injury: does the person have cover; what kind of injury is it
--    and which Account pays; and what weekly compensation is payable after
--    the first five weeks?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1 and 3. Claims (Goal 2), disputes (Goal 4),
-- levies (Goal 5) and offences (Goal 6) answer their own questions in their
-- modules.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `ACC position` HAS
    `an accident`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a treatment injury`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `has cover`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `class of injury`                                IS AN `Injury class`
    `Account that pays`                              IS AN Account
    `weekly compensation after 5 weeks`              IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 20-35, 166-228; Schedule 1 cls 32, 34, 42, 46, 51; ss 119-122
GIVEN c IS AN `Injury case`
GIVETH AN `ACC position`
`the ACC position for` c MEANS
    `ACC position` WITH
        `an accident`                                    IS `accident` c
        `a treatment injury`                             IS `a treatment injury` (c's `treatment`)
        `has cover`                                      IS `covered` c
        `class of injury`                                IS `the class of` c
        `Account that pays`                              IS `the Account that pays for` (`the class of` c) `, claimant` (c's `status`)
        `weekly compensation after 5 weeks`              IS `weekly compensation for` c

GIVEN c IS AN `Injury case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `accident` c IF
    `an accident under s 25, occurrence` (c's `injury`'s `occurrence`) `, treatment:` (c's `treatment`'s `caused by treatment`)

GIVEN c IS AN `Injury case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` c IF
    `has cover, injury` (c's `injury`) `, accident:` (`accident` c) `, treatment injury:` (`a treatment injury` (c's `treatment`))

GIVEN c IS AN `Injury case`
GIVETH AN `Injury class`
`the class of` c MEANS
    `the class of injury, treatment injury:` (`a treatment injury` (c's `treatment`)) `, for a work injury:` (c's `treatment`'s `the treatment was for a work-related injury`) `, at work:` (c's `work circumstance`) `, vehicle:` (`the vehicle involvement that counts under s 35, harm` (c's `injury`'s `harm`) `, vehicle` (c's `vehicle`)) `, work gradual process:` (c's `injury`'s `cause` EQUALS `a work-related gradual process, disease or infection`)

-- Weekly compensation is worked out here only for an employee in permanent
-- employment (Schedule 1 cl 34). A non-earner has no entitlement under
-- Schedule 1 cl 32 (only an earner, or a potential earner under cl 47, is
-- entitled), so the answer is 0. For other earners and potential earners the
-- formula is in cls 36-47 and is carried as text, so the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN c IS AN `Injury case`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`weekly compensation for` c MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `covered` c THEN JUST 0
           IF `the entitlement is barred by` (c's `disentitlement`) `, entitlement` `weekly compensation (Schedule 1 Part 2)` THEN JUST 0
           IF c's `status` EQUALS `an employee` THEN
               JUST (`the weekly compensation on weekly earnings of`
                        (`the weekly earnings after the low-earner rule,` (c's `earnings`) `, calculated` (`the weekly earnings of a permanent employee,` (c's `earnings`) `, in week` 6))
                        `, earning after incapacity` (c's `earnings`'s `earnings after incapacity, per week`)
                        `, maximum` `the maximum weekly compensation in the Act`)
           IF c's `status` EQUALS `a non-earner` THEN JUST 0
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
